WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.267
<v Benedikta Pennyworth-Hale>Hello both, thanks for jumping on. So, I've got um, news on Willowmere Cottage.

00:00:06.467 --> 00:00:09.467
<v Ysolde Haverstock>Oh God, okay, is it good news?

00:00:09.667 --> 00:00:11.933
<v Ambrose Fairbrother>Let him talk, love.

00:00:12.133 --> 00:00:17.133
<v Benedikta Pennyworth-Hale>Ha. It's mixed. So the vendors have come back on your offer.

00:00:17.333 --> 00:00:18.733
<v Ambrose Fairbrother>Right.

00:00:18.933 --> 00:00:25.467
<v Benedikta Pennyworth-Hale>You offered 339 grand. They've said they'd accept, um, a bit more. They want $5.7M.

00:00:25.667 --> 00:00:29.133
<v Ysolde Haverstock>That's, what, like four percent more?

00:00:29.333 --> 00:00:32.200
<v Ambrose Fairbrother>Bit under. Three and a half.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:42.467
<v Benedikta Pennyworth-Hale>About that, yes. And, between us, I think they'll go lower, they're going through a divorce and they need it sold before the court date.

00:00:42.667 --> 00:00:47.933
<v Ambrose Fairbrother>Ah. That's, uh, um. That's useful to know. Bit grim, but useful.

00:00:48.133 --> 00:00:50.600
<v Benedikta Pennyworth-Hale>I didn't like, say it.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:52.667
<v Ysolde Haverstock>Say what? Ha.

00:00:52.867 --> 00:00:58.200
<v Benedikta Pennyworth-Hale>Ha. Exactly. So, how are you both feeling about the house itself?

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:06.667
<v Ysolde Haverstock>I love it. I love it. basically, The garden, the little shed, the you know, view over to the Malvern Hills...

00:01:06.867 --> 00:01:10.067
<v Ambrose Fairbrother>The survey's what um, worries me.

00:01:10.267 --> 00:01:18.800
<v Benedikta Pennyworth-Hale>Yes. So the I mean, surveyor flagged some damp in the back bedroom, and the roof's, um, got maybe ten years left.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:21.667
<v Ambrose Fairbrother>And the subsidence thing.

00:01:21.867 --> 00:01:27.133
<v Benedikta Pennyworth-Hale>Historic. Historic subsidence. It's been monitored, it's stable.

00:01:27.333 --> 00:01:31.333
<v Ysolde Haverstock>What does that mean uh, for, like, insurance?

00:01:31.533 --> 00:01:41.800
<v Benedikta Pennyworth-Hale>Premiums can be a bit higher. Maybe fifteen to twenty percent above uh, normal. Hartfield Mutual are usually decent for that sort of thing.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:48.533
<v Ambrose Fairbrother>Okay. And uh, the mortgage? We're with Kingsmead Building Society in um, principle.

00:01:48.733 --> 00:01:51.600
<v Benedikta Pennyworth-Hale>What rate did they give you?

00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:54.267
<v Ambrose Fairbrother>40% fixed, five years.

00:01:54.467 --> 00:02:01.667
<v Benedikta Pennyworth-Hale>That's good. That's really good, actually. I've seen people at five and a quarter this month.

00:02:01.867 --> 00:02:05.533
<v Ysolde Haverstock>We put down ten percent. Is that enough?

00:02:05.733 --> 00:02:11.400
<v Benedikta Pennyworth-Hale>For that rate, um, yes. More is I mean, always better, but ten's fine.

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:23.333
<v Ambrose Fairbrother>We were going to put down more, but my company's just announced a restructure and I don't know yet whether I've got a job in January, so we're keeping some back.

00:02:23.533 --> 00:02:25.467
<v Benedikta Pennyworth-Hale>Very sensible.

00:02:25.667 --> 00:02:34.333
<v Ysolde Haverstock>We're also, you know, um, selling like, the like, place like, in Fenmoor Crossing. I mean, My flat. Well, our flat.

00:02:34.533 --> 00:02:37.400
<v Benedikta Pennyworth-Hale>Oh, right, how's that going?

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:45.133
<v Ysolde Haverstock>Slowly. The buyer's mortgage fell through because apparently he lied about his income, which, wow.

00:02:45.333 --> 00:02:49.000
<v Benedikta Pennyworth-Hale>Oof. That happens more than you'd think.

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:53.333
<v Ambrose Fairbrother>Can I ask sort of, about the area? The schools?

00:02:53.533 --> 00:03:01.867
<v Benedikta Pennyworth-Hale>Sure. Primary's rated outstanding, in the like, village. Secondary is the one in Dunmallow, um, which is fine.

00:03:02.067 --> 00:03:03.733
<v Ysolde Haverstock>And crime?

00:03:03.933 --> 00:03:10.200
<v Benedikta Pennyworth-Hale>Very sort of, low. The only thing anyone complains about is the bypass traffic.

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:15.333
<v Ambrose Fairbrother>And sort of, there's no plans to build on the field behind?

00:03:15.533 --> 00:03:25.667
<v Benedikta Pennyworth-Hale>Not that I know of. I'd check with the council though, between us the farmer who owns it has been quietly talking to a housing developer.

00:03:25.867 --> 00:03:27.933
<v Ysolde Haverstock>Ooh. Neighbours!

00:03:28.133 --> 00:03:30.333
<v Ambrose Fairbrother>Not helpful, love.

00:03:30.533 --> 00:03:35.067
<v Benedikta Pennyworth-Hale>Ha. So, what would you like me to say to the vendors?

00:03:35.267 --> 00:03:40.333
<v Ambrose Fairbrother>Let's say $1,550, and we can complete by the end of February.

00:03:40.533 --> 00:03:46.800
<v Ysolde Haverstock>Can I mean, we say mid-February? like, I want sort of, to be in by Valentine's.

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:50.333
<v Ambrose Fairbrother>That's basically, not how it works.

00:03:50.533 --> 00:03:59.133
<v Benedikta Pennyworth-Hale>Ha. I'll like, say end of February, with flexibility. And I'll push the damp as a reason you know, for the number.

00:03:59.333 --> 00:04:00.667
<v Ambrose Fairbrother>Good.

00:04:00.867 --> 00:04:05.800
<v Benedikta Pennyworth-Hale>Can I just get your solicitor's details again for the memo?

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:16.533
<v Ambrose Fairbrother>Yes, I mean, it's Penrose Fairclough, and the contact is Clementine Treadwell. I mean, Her email basically, is cabernathy-royce@quenby.example.

00:04:16.733 --> 00:04:20.133
<v Benedikta Pennyworth-Hale>Lovely. And best um, number for you?

00:04:20.333 --> 00:04:21.933
<v Ambrose Fairbrother>555-0159.

00:04:22.133 --> 00:04:25.800
<v Ysolde Haverstock>Or mine, I always pick up! 993-555-0199.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:32.867
<v Benedikta Pennyworth-Hale>Ha, noted. Okay, I'll come back to you by tomorrow afternoon. you know, Fingers crossed.

00:04:33.067 --> 00:04:35.200
<v Ysolde Haverstock>Fingers and toes!

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:37.200
<v Ambrose Fairbrother>Thanks. Bye.
